Subject: Spell XGETBV as an instruction instead of raw opcode bytes
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/libwebp-1.4.0.patch

Fil-C validates inline instructions and supports xgetbv with these register
constraints; raw .byte directives cannot be validated. With libwebp 1.6 the
lossless decoder's DSP init reaches this probe (VP8LNew -> x86CPUInfo),
which libtiff's webp_lossless tiffcp test exercises.

--- a/src/dsp/cpu.c
+++ b/src/dsp/cpu.c
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ static WEBP_INLINE uint64_t xgetbv(void) {
   uint32_t eax, edx;
   // Use the raw opcode for xgetbv for compatibility with older toolchains.
   __asm__ volatile (
-    ".byte 0x0f, 0x01, 0xd0\n"
+    "xgetbv\n"
     : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx) : "c" (ecx));
   return ((uint64_t)edx << 32) | eax;
 }
